        ("Counter-Strike", "Minh Le and Jess Cliffe's 1999 Half-Life mod became the longest-running competitive shooter on PC; Half-Life, the game it was built from, is here instead."),
        ("Final Fantasy XIV", "Its 2013 relaunch rescued a failed online game and became one of the best stories in the genre, but World of Warcraft is our one online role-playing game."),
        ("Planescape: Torment", "The 1999 role-playing game that put writing ahead of combat; Disco Elysium carries the same idea and is far easier to play today."),
        ("Spelunky", "Derek Yu's 2008 platformer brought roguelike rules to action games, and Rogue, FTL, Hades and Balatro already carry that line."),
        ("Genshin Impact", "The 2020 free-to-play hit from China's miHoYo is one of the most-played games of its decade, but it is still changing and built around paid random draws, which made it hard to judge as a finished game."),
